  "answer_text": "There are **three ways** to change a `<span>`'s color on mouse over: using **CSS**, **inline HTML events**, or **JavaScript**. Here's how to do each:\n\n---\n\n## \u2705 Method 1: CSS `:hover` (Recommended)\n\nThis is the simplest and cleanest approach.\n\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n  <head>\n    <style>\n      span:hover {\n        color: red;\n      }\n    </style>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <span>Hover over me!</span>\n  </body>\n</html>\n```\n\nIf you need to change the text color on mouseover for all elements of a certain type, then using CSS is the best option.\n\nYou can also target a **specific span** using a class or ID:\n\n```css\nspan#mySpan:hover {\n  color: red;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## \u2705 Method 2: Inline `onmouseover` / `onmouseout` HTML Attributes\n\nYou can use HTML event attributes directly on the element:\n\n```html\n<span\n  onmouseover=\"this.style.color='red';\"\n  onmouseout=\"this.style.color='black';\"\n>\n  Hover over me!\n</span>\n```\n\n---\n\n## \u2705 Method 3: JavaScript Event Listeners\n\nIf you need to change the text color on a mouseover for a specific element, or if you need to change the text color dynamically, then using JavaScript is the best option.\n\nThe `onmouseover` event is triggered when the user hovers over an element with the mouse.\n\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n  <body>\n    <span id=\"mySpan\">Hover over me!</span>\n\n    <script>\n      const span = document.getElementById(\"mySpan\");\n\n      span.addEventListener(\"mouseover\", function () {\n        span.style.color = \"red\";\n      });\n\n      span.addEventListener(\"mouseout\", function () {\n        span.style.color = \"black\";\n      });\n    </script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n```\n\nA `mouseover` event is added to the element, changing its text color when the user hovers over it. A `mouseout` event is also added to change its text color back to the default when the user moves their cursor out.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83c\udfc6 Which Method Should You Use?\n\n| Method | Best For |\n|---|---|\n| **CSS `:hover`** | Simple, static color changes \u2014 always preferred |\n| **Inline HTML** | Quick prototyping / simple cases |\n| **JavaScript** | Dynamic or conditional color changes |\n\nFor most use cases, **CSS `:hover`** is the recommended approach as it keeps styling separate from logic and is the most performant.",
